Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0003.
DeepSeek-V4.1 wo_a on SM12x (GB10): DeepGEMM's MXFP8 bmm and fp8_einsum are datacenter-Blackwell only, so wo_a fell back to
EmulationMxfp8LinearKernel (BF16 dequant at load + BF16 bmm: 2x the bytes and the memory). Sm12xMarlinMxfp8BmmLinearKernel
keeps the FP8 weight, Marlin-packs each group once at load and runs one Marlin MXFP8 (W8A16) GEMM per group: 21.4 us per
1024x4096 group at m=1, ~203 GB/s, vs 65.8 us (~66 GB/s) for the CUTLASS MXFP8 GEMM, distinct weights cycled from DRAM
(scripts/bench/linear_dram_bench.py, idle GB10). deep_gemm_fp8_o_proj routes to it after the inverse RoPE.
Test: patches/tests/test_sm12x_mxfp8_bmm.py.

